          "text": "Left knee pain history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Left anterior/medial knee ache described as like a bruise under the kneecap, beginning about 2–3 weeks after lifting boxes during a big weekend. Pain 3–4/10 at baseline, up to 6/10 on stairs, especially descending. Worse with stairs, squatting, and standing from a chair after prolonged sitting; settles with rest. No night pain or significant morning stiffness over 10 minutes. No clear trauma, prior similar episode, true locking, giving way, or catching. Patient is unsure about swelling, saying it may be puffy in the evenings. Fully weight-bearing and mobilising unaided. Patient thinks a new higher desk chair with legs dangling may be contributing."
      }
    },
